<title>NETHERLANDS: Dutch bonds end mixed, long end well off highs.</title>
<headline>Dutch bonds end mixed, long end well off highs.</headline>
<text>
<p>1635 GMT - Dutch bonds end mostly firmer but well off early highs as bunds draw back late. Short end loses some ground.</p>
<p>Finance ministry closes new 10-year tap issue after raising total of 7.5 billion guilders. Some feel may be reopened later to get bond up to 10 billion benchmark size.</p>
<p>* 6.25 July 1998 104.11/19,(-0.03) bid yld 3.31 pct.</p>
<p>* Sept 2001 117.34/44 (-0.02), bid yld 4.52 pct.</p>
<p>* Jan 2006 103.08 (+0.08), bid yield 5.55 pct.</p>
<p>* New 5.75 2007s average price 100.85, yield 5.64.</p>
<p>* 10-yr yld spread vs April 2006 bund out to -14 bp from -10.</p>
<p>* Jan 2023s 113.74/94 (+0.30), 6.40 pct yield.</p>
